---
export const prerender = false;
import LegalDocument from '../components/LegalDocument.astro';
---

<LegalDocument
  title="Refund Policy"
  eyebrow="A fair way to change your mind"
  description="ImageToURL Pro cancellation and refund rules, including the 14-day first-purchase refund."
  intro="We want the purchase decision to feel low-risk. This policy explains when ImageToURL Pro payments may be refunded and how to request one."
>
  <section>
    <h2>1. 14-day first-purchase refund</h2>
    <p>
      You may request a full refund of your first ImageToURL Pro subscription payment within 14 calendar
      days of purchase. This applies to the first monthly or annual payment for a new customer account.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may deny or limit a refund where there is evidence of fraud, repeated refund abuse, a material
      violation of our policies, or unusually high consumption intended to exploit the refund offer.
      Mandatory consumer rights always take priority.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Renewals and other refunds</h2>
    <p>
      Renewal payments are generally non-refundable once the new billing period begins. If you forgot to
      cancel, contact us within seven days of renewal. We will review the request fairly, considering use
      of the service after renewal and any rights that apply where you live.
    </p>
    <p>
      Duplicate charges, incorrect charges, or charges made after a confirmed cancellation will be
      investigated and refunded where verified. We may also issue full or partial refunds where the
      service was materially unavailable or did not match the purchased description.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Cancellation is different from a refund</h2>
    <p>
      Canceling stops the next automatic renewal. Unless a refund is approved or law requires otherwise,
      your Pro workspace remains active through the end of the paid billing period and unused time is not
      automatically prorated.
    </p>
    <p>
      A storage pack purchased with the first Pro checkout is included when that first purchase qualifies
      for a refund. Later prorated add-on charges are normally non-refundable once capacity is provisioned,
      except for duplicate or incorrect charges, service failure, or rights required by law.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can cancel and manage payment details through the secure Paddle customer portal available from
      your Pro account settings.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. How to request a refund</h2>
    <p>Use either of these methods:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Visit <a href="https://paddle.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener">paddle.net</a> and provide the email address and transaction details used at checkout; or</li>
      <li>Email <a href="mailto:blog.boopul@gmail.com?subject=ImageToURL%20Pro%20refund%20request">blog.boopul@gmail.com</a> with your account email, transaction or receipt number, purchase date, and reason for the request.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Do not send card numbers or sensitive payment credentials by email.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Processing and access after a refund</h2>
    <p>
      Paddle issues approved refunds to the original payment method. Bank and payment-network processing
      times vary. When a full refund is completed, paid access may end immediately.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before requesting a refund, download any files you need. A refund does not require us to continue
      providing paid storage or delivery after Pro access ends.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Consumer rights</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing in this policy removes statutory withdrawal, refund, or consumer-protection rights that
      cannot legally be waived. Where Paddle’s buyer terms or applicable law provides stronger rights,
      those stronger rights apply.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalDocument>
